    "copy_en": "A labyrinth isn't a maze — there are no wrong turns. One path winds all the way in and all the way back out; you can't get lost, you can only keep walking. Look at how this is strung: one single cord through every bead, one unbroken path. That's the whole promise. You don't have to figure out the route — you just have to not stop.",
