    "copy_en": "Five elements — wood feeds fire, fire makes earth, earth yields metal, metal carries water, water grows wood again. Written down in the *Book of Documents* over two thousand years ago. The point was never the five things; it's that each one *becomes* the next, with no last one. Strung in a closed circle, in that exact order, it does the only thing the idea ever meant: it never arrives anywhere, and it never runs out.",
    "hook_zh": "串成一个合上的圈、按这个顺序，它就做成了这意思唯一想表达的事：它哪儿都不抵达，也永远用不完。",
